(external verifier improves generation). It is NOT supported: condition_accuracy shows
{carnot:0.867, rfg:0.3, unguided:0.3, entrgi:0.3} -- all THREE controls bit-identical at 0.3,
i.e. RFG/EntRGi did not actually apply guidance (no-ops). The TAUTOLOGY flag (carnot-rfg ==
carnot-unguided, fires on-disk too) is a TRUE-positive correctly revealing RFG==unguided, so
'Carnot beats the model's self-guidance' is really 'Carnot beats a no-op'. Keep it quarantined
(unlike the exp4257 reproduction false-positive that was rescued). Second concern: the exp4292
partial-state scorer AUROC=0.966 may inflate the Carnot arm (leak re-check needed). The §5
in-generation thesis stays OPEN; the verifier's proven value remains SELECTION (cross-family +
cross-generator) + efficiency. .398 must use differentiated controls + re-verify no scorer leak.

